  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper introduces Adaptive Hamming Weight Operator QAOA (AHWO-QAOA), a constraint-preserving mixer for QAOA that keeps the state within the feasible subspace. In noiseless simulations on constrained portfolio optimization and two‑jet clustering problems with 6–20 qubits, AHWO-QAOA achieves 100% constraint satisfaction, converges in ~30 iterations versus ~90–410 for penalty-QAOA on a 12‑qubit case, and uses roughly 470 gates at 20 qubits compared with ~1270 for a 5‑layer penalty-based QAOA baseline.",
